.Dd September 27, 2026
.Dt SRV 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm srv
.Nd serve the current directory over HTTP
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl i Ar duration
.Op Fl t Ar rate
.Op Ar port
.Nm
.Fl h | Fl -help
.Nm
.Fl V | Fl -version
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
starts an HTTP server that serves the files in the current working directory.
It listens on all IPv4 interfaces on
.Ar port ,
which defaults to 8000.
.Pp
A request for a directory serves its
.Pa index.html
if one exists, and otherwise returns a generated listing of the directory.
A request for a directory without a trailing slash is redirected to the
same path with a trailing slash.
The
.Ql ..\&
and
.Ql .\&
path segments are ignored, so files outside the current directory cannot be
reached.
.Pp
Only
.Cm GET
and
.Cm HEAD
requests are supported.
The content type is chosen from the file name extension.
Each connection is handled on its own thread and closed after the response.
.Pp
Each request is logged to standard output in the same format as
Python's
.Ql http.server
module.
.Pp
The options are as follows:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl i , Fl -idle Ar duration
Stop the server when no request has been made and no connection has been
open for
.Ar duration .
A plain number is a number of seconds.
Units can be given as in
.Ql 30s ,
.Ql 10m ,
.Ql 1h
or
.Ql 1h 30m .
.It Fl t , Fl -throttle Ar rate
Limit the bandwidth to simulate a slow connection.
The limit is shared by all connections, as on a real network link.
.Ar rate
is either a preset, which also delays each response, or a number of bits
per second with an optional
.Ql k ,
.Ql m
or
.Ql g
suffix, such as
.Ql 500k
or
.Ql 1.5m .
The presets are:
.Pp
.Bl -tag -width "edge" -compact
.It 56k
56 kbit/s, 150 ms latency
.It edge
240 kbit/s, 400 ms latency
.It 3g
750 kbit/s, 300 ms latency
.It 4g
9 Mbit/s, 100 ms latency
.El
.It Fl h , Fl -help
Print a usage summary and exit.
.It Fl V , Fl -version
Print the version and exit.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Nm
runs until it is interrupted, or exits 0 when the
.Fl i
duration has passed without requests.
It exits 1 if the server cannot be started, for example because
.Ar port
is already in use, and 2 if the arguments are invalid.
.Sh EXAMPLES
Serve the current directory on port 8000:
.Pp
.Dl $ srv
.Pp
Serve the current directory on port 9000:
.Pp
.Dl $ srv 9000
.Pp
Serve on port 8000 and stop after ten minutes without requests:
.Pp
.Dl $ srv -i 10m
.Pp
Serve on port 9000 as if over a 3G connection:
.Pp
.Dl $ srv -t 3g 9000
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr python3 1
.Sh CAVEATS
.Nm
has no access control and serves every file in the current directory to
anyone who can reach the port.
Do not run it on untrusted networks.
